#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I -B -X pycache_prefix=/dev/null
"""The Author's clean-room gate (spec 000 FR-041; plan §11, §19; ADR 0017; research.md R-23, R-35, R-36).

    tools/gates/gate [--host] [--prove] [--otlp-url URL] REF
    tools/gates/gate --contract-replay FILE

Run it directly from the main working tree, never through make: a planted GNUmakefile would shadow the Makefile.
Project code never runs outside a container in the Author's terminal. On the host the gate runs only git, docker,
gitleaks, and the main working tree's own code (this file, tools/gates/*.py, corpus/tools/check_corpus.py, and
deploy/agents-engine/engine.sh), each with an environment it builds itself. The commit under test is data there.

1. Export. REF resolves once to a commit SHA, which every later step and the merge use. Every git call runs with
   GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1. A ref under refs/replace stops the gate, since the Author's merge would honor it. So do
   .git/info/attributes and submodules, which git archive would apply or skip. `git archive` exports the commit,
   tarfile's data filter extracts it, and the export must hash to the tree its commit object names, the object
   rehashed against its SHA. Anything short of that proof stops the gate. The export is read-only from then on.
2. Makefiles. The container phase's make would read a GNUmakefile or makefile before the Makefile, so the export may
   hold neither, or exactly main's GNUmakefile and no makefile. Anything else stops the container phase.
3. Container phase, on this machine's engine (plan §11: the devcontainer build needs Ubuntu's mirrors). The
   devcontainer image is built from the export's .devcontainer/ and tagged by that directory's tree hash. A copy of
   the export gets `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, with the network. Then, each with `--network none`: make lint,
   validate-config, test, evals, redteam-suite, and matrix (stage H). Every container drops all capabilities, sets
   no-new-privileges, and runs as the Author's uid on that copy.
4. Host phase:
   - githooks: the installed hooks match the main tree's .claude/git-hooks/, core.hooksPath is unset,
     gc.packRefs is false, and main is a loose ref, as `make githooks-check` has it;
   - toolchain: tools/gates/toolchain_check.py against the export's pins;
   - policy: tools/gates/compose_policy.py --root <export>;
   - corpus: corpus/tools/check_corpus.py over the export's corpus, with the Author's denylist, which must exist;
     loaded into this process, which runs with PY_HOST's flags, since the script reads only its own tree;
   - gitleaks over $(git merge-base main SHA)..SHA, with the main tree's .gitleaks.toml (--config), a fresh empty
     --gitleaks-ignore-path, and --ignore-gitleaks-allow. It refuses while a .gitleaksignore at the main tree
     could hold an entry (research.md R-36);
   - image: the compose images, built on the agents' engine (198.18.0.1:2376) with the Author's certificate, and
     only after the policy passed, because an unvetted build could read host files into the engine;
   - matrix-e: stage E, when the branch touches deploy/agents-engine/ or .claude/settings.json. It is Heavy, so it
     waits (PENDING) for --prove, which runs deploy/agents-engine/engine.sh prove;
   - agent-config-evals: the behavioral tier, when the branch touches CLAUDE.md, REVIEW.md, .claude/,
     evals/agent-config/ (its history aside), or the Claude Code pin. T094 adds the tier; until then this step is
     SKIP naming it, and once evals/agent-config/behavioral.py exists it fails until it is wired here.
5. eval-history: each history entry the branch adds is posted once to prod's x004 as the h4.devtime.eval.* gauges
   (contracts/telemetry.md §4.4): OTLP/JSON, stdlib, no proxy, timestamped at the post. An entry needs "verdict"
   ("pass" or "fail"), "notional_cost_usd" (a number), and "tokens" with "input", "output", "cache_read", and
   "cache_creation" (integers). A malformed entry fails; a collector that doesn't answer is a WARN.
6. Summary. One line for the merge commit's message, and the merge command, by SHA, with replace objects off.

--host skips the container phase (plan §19: the devcontainer image won't build), and every summary line says
DEGRADED. Lint, tests, the scaffolds, and stage H then run nowhere: never on the host.

--contract-replay FILE is make contract-live's replay (contracts/provider-adapter.md §5.3): the container phase over
`git archive HEAD`, with FILE mounted read-only, running `vitest run test/contract/replay.test.ts` in the gateway
with H4_CONTRACT_RECORDING set and --network none. It passes only when the replay passed tests under the
recording's own name ("recorded live: <adapter>"), so a replay that never read FILE can't pass.

Statuses are make check's (PASS, SKIP, PLANNED, PENDING, FAIL), plus WARN for telemetry that didn't arrive.
Exit 0 with no FAIL or PENDING; 1 otherwise, or when the export's proof fails; 2 when the gate refuses to start.
"""

